IMPORT prelude

-- Radiation Protection Act 2007 (Singapore) -- what needs a licence or the Director-General's approval and what it costs not to have
-- one (ss 6, 7, 12, 13, 15), the presumption that stored residue is radioactive waste (s 13(3)), records (s 16), confidentiality
-- (s 18), refusing entry to inspectors (s 45(2)), appeals (s 46), liability of officers (s 50), the residual penalty (s 52) and the
-- cap on composition sums (s 53).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RPA2007.txt. The deposit says
-- it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amending Act annotated in the text is 15/2019
-- (Second Schedule), and most annotations are 20/2014.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 8 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the controls a business, clinic or
-- laboratory actually meets. Not encoded: administration (ss 4, 5), licence procedure and the Director-General's discretion (s 8),
-- the duties of licensees to employees and third parties (ss 10, 11, which carry no express penalty -- see s 52), the
-- Director-General's own disposal power (s 14), the Safeguards information notices (s 17), the inspection and warrant machinery
-- (ss 19-27), the nuclear material offences of Part 8A and the Second Schedule, arrest, search and forfeiture (ss 40-43), false
-- statements (s 44), exemptions and regulations (ss 55, 57). The "prescribed level" of radioactivity that makes an article
-- radioactive material (s 2) is left to regulations, none of which were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Radiation Protection Act 2007 -- control`

DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `importing or exporting radioactive material`
    `possessing or using radioactive material`
    `selling radioactive material`
    `transporting radioactive material`
    `importing or exporting an irradiating apparatus`
    `possessing or using an irradiating apparatus`
    `manufacturing an irradiating apparatus`
    `selling an irradiating apparatus`
    `disposing of an irradiating apparatus`
    `disposing of radioactive waste`
    `accumulating radioactive waste`
    `transporting radioactive waste`

§§ `6, 7, 12, 13, 15 -- licence or approval`

-- s 6(1): "A person must not, except under and in accordance with a licence" (a) import or export, (b) keep, possess, control or use,
-- (c) manufacture, sell or otherwise deal in, or (d) transport, any radioactive material. (2): fine up to $100,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 7(1): the same for irradiating apparatus -- (a) import or export, (b) keep, possess, control or use, (c) manufacture or produce,
-- (d) sell or deal. (5): $100,000 or 5 years. Note: s 7(1) does not list TRANSPORT of irradiating apparatus.
-- s 7(4): "A person must not dispose of any irradiating apparatus, whether in a working condition or otherwise, without the prior
-- written approval of the Director-General." (6): $50,000 or 12 months.
-- s 12(1): radioactive waste may not be disposed of "except with the prior written approval of the Director-General"; (2) an offence
-- only if "without reasonable excuse": $50,000 or 12 months.
-- s 13(1): the same for ACCUMULATING radioactive waste on any premises -- but (2) no further approval is needed where a s 12 disposal
-- approval requires or permits accumulation with a view to disposal. (4): $50,000 or 12 months. No reasonable-excuse words.
-- s 15: the same for TRANSPORTING radioactive waste. $50,000 or 12 months. No reasonable-excuse words.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct needs a licence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `disposing of an irradiating apparatus` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `disposing of radioactive waste` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `accumulating radioactive waste` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `transporting radioactive waste` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `holds a licence covering it` IS A BOOLEAN, `has prior written approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a disposal approval permitting accumulation` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence` IF
    IF `the conduct needs a licence`
        `the conduct`
    THEN NOT `holds a licence covering it`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the conduct`
        WHEN `disposing of radioactive waste` THEN (NOT `has prior written approval`) AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)
        WHEN `accumulating radioactive waste` THEN (NOT `has prior written approval`) AND (NOT `has a disposal approval permitting accumulation`)
        OTHERWISE NOT `has prior written approval`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the conduct needs a licence` `the conduct` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the conduct needs a licence` `the conduct` THEN 60 ELSE 12

-- s 7(2): "Every person who sells any irradiating apparatus must immediately give notice of the sale to the Director-General", with
-- the buyer's name, address and prescribed particulars; (3) every BUYER must likewise immediately give notice of the purchase, with the
-- seller's particulars. (6): $50,000 or 12 months. Both sides of the sale must notify.
GIVEN `sold or bought an irradiating apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN, `immediately notified the Director-General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to notify the sale or purchase is an offence` IF
    `sold or bought an irradiating apparatus` AND (NOT `immediately notified the Director-General`)

§§ `13(3) -- presumption of radioactive waste`

-- s 13(3): where radioactive material is produced, kept or used on premises and a substance arising from it is (a) "accumulated in any
-- part of the premises appropriated for the purpose" and (b) "retained there for a period of 3 or more months", that substance is,
-- "unless the contrary is proved", presumed (c) to be radioactive waste and (d) accumulated with a view to subsequent disposal.
GIVEN `radioactive material is produced, kept or used on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the substance is accumulated in a part appropriated for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months retained` IS A NUMBER, `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substance is presumed to be radioactive waste awaiting disposal` IF
        `radioactive material is produced, kept or used on the premises`
    AND `the substance is accumulated in a part appropriated for the purpose`
    AND `months retained` AT LEAST 3
    AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

§§ `16 -- records and reports`

-- s 16(1): "Every licensee, and every person who has been granted any approval by the Director-General under this Act" must keep
-- prescribed records and give prescribed or directed periodic and special reports. (2): "without reasonable excuse" -- $10,000 or
-- 3 months.
GIVEN `is a licensee or approval holder` IS A BOOLEAN, `kept the records and made the reports` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the records failure is an offence` IF
    `is a licensee or approval holder` AND (NOT `kept the records and made the reports`) AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `18 -- confidentiality`

-- s 18(1): every person exercising a function under the Act must keep confidential information obtained under it "concerning the
-- affairs of another person", including trade secrets. (2) it may be disclosed (a) with consent; (b) for the purposes of the Act, the
-- Safeguards Agreement or the Nuclear Material Convention; (c) for a criminal investigation or proceedings; (d) as required by a court,
-- tribunal or person with lawful authority; (e) for "an emergency involving public safety or ensuring the security of Singapore";
-- (f) if already in the public domain. (3): $6,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `with the consent of the person concerned`
    `for the purposes of the Act or the Safeguards Agreement`
    `for a criminal investigation`
    `under a court order`
    `for a public safety emergency`
    `of information already public`
    `to a journalist who asks`
    `to the licensee's commercial rival`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `to a journalist who asks` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to the licensee's commercial rival` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `45(2) -- refusing entry`

-- s 45(1): obstructing, hindering, resisting or deceiving an authorised officer or IAEA inspector -- $50,000 or 12 months. (2):
-- "Nothing in subsection (1) applies to a refusal to give consent to entry" by an inspector or officer "not acting pursuant to a
-- warrant" under s 25, 26 or 41. Without a warrant, an occupier may say no.
GIVEN `the inspector acts under a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing consent to entry can be obstruction` IF
    `the inspector acts under a warrant`

§§ `46 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- s 46(1): a person dissatisfied with a decision of the Director-General "under section 8, 14 or 15" may appeal to the Minister in
-- writing "within 30 days of the communication" of the decision. (4): the Minister's decision is final. Decisions under s 12 (waste
-- disposal approval), s 13 (accumulation) and s 7(4) (apparatus disposal) are NOT listed. Reading "within 30 days" to include day 30
-- is an inference.
GIVEN `the section decided under` IS A NUMBER, `days since the decision was communicated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister lies` IF
        (`the section decided under` EQUALS 8 OR `the section decided under` EQUALS 14 OR `the section decided under` EQUALS 15)
    AND `days since the decision was communicated` AT MOST 30

§§ `50 -- officers of bodies corporate`

-- s 50(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer; or
-- (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer's part", the officer as well as the body corporate is guilty. (3), (4): the same
-- for partners and officers of unincorporated associations.
GIVEN `the body committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence is attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the body committed an offence` AND (`the officer consented or connived` OR `the offence is attributable to the officer's neglect`)

§§ `52 -- penalty not otherwise provided`

-- s 52: contravening a provision with no express penalty -- (a) where the contravention "endanger[s] or is likely to endanger human
-- life", $50,000 or 12 months; (b) otherwise $10,000 or 3 months. This is the penalty that reaches the licensee duties in ss 10 and 11
-- (an inference: neither section states its own penalty).
GIVEN `endangers human life` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residual maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `endangers human life` THEN 50000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `endangers human life` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residual maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `endangers human life` THEN 12 ELSE 3

§§ `53 -- composition`

-- s 53(1): the Director-General may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting a sum not exceeding "the
-- lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (b) $15,000. Which offences are
-- compoundable is left to regulations (s 53(3)); none were retrieved.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 15000
